<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaret I of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1353–<a href="/years/1412">1412</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Margaret I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaret I was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark">Valdemar IV of Denmark</a> and widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-vi-of-norway">Haakon VI of Norway</a>, she governed Denmark from 1375 and Norway from 1380, and won Sweden by defeating King Albert of Mecklenburg in 1389. In 1397 she had her great-nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a> crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a>, creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Margaret I of Denmark" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob Truedson Demitz assisted by Emil Eikner for Ristesson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Margaret_of_Denmark,_Norway_%26_Sweden_(1389)_effigy_2010_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
